.TH CLEANUP 1 "2026-11-19" "cleanup 0.1.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cleanup \- reclaim disk space from dev artifacts, stale worktrees and retired tools without deleting work
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcleanup\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIROOT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcleanup\fR scans one root (default \fI~/Projects\fR) once, proposes regenerable build artifacts, stale linked git worktrees and leftovers of tools you have marked as retired, and inspects every candidate before anything can be deleted. It runs as a dry run unless \fB\-d\fR is given.
.SH MODE
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview only; delete nothing (default; the last of \-n/\-d wins)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-delete\fR
Delete selected items (needs TUI confirmation or \-f/\-\-force)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Skip the TUI and confirmation when deleting
.SH SELECTION
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR
Directory to scan (default ~/Projects)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Config file merged over the defaults (default ~/.config/cleanup/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-only\fR \fIIDS\fR
Run only these cleaner ids (comma\-separated or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-exclude\fR \fIIDS\fR
Skip these cleaner ids (comma\-separated or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-venvs\fR
Python: include marker\-verified virtualenvs
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-modules\fR
Node: include node_modules
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-retired\fR \fIIDS\fR
Treat these configured tool ids as retired for this run
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-age\fR \fIDAYS\fR
Minimum idle age for worktrees and retired tools (default from config)
.SH SAFETY OVERRIDES
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-include\-dirty\fR
UNSAFE: also delete git trees with uncommitted changes, untracked files or an unreachable detached HEAD
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Plain\-text output instead of the interactive TUI
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-show\-skipped\fR
Show skipped and protected items
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-group\-by\fR \fIMODE\fR
Initial TUI grouping: cleaner or project (default cleaner)
.SH INFORMATION
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\-categories\fR
List cleaners and retired tools, then exit
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-print\-config\fR
Print the default config, then exit
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-print\-man\fR
Print the man page (roff), then exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help, then exit
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version, then exit
.SH SAFETY
Every candidate passes one inspection step that fails closed: any error skips the item.
.IP \(bu 2
Git\-tracked files are never deleted.
.IP \(bu 2
A git tree is skipped when it has uncommitted changes, untracked files, an unreachable detached HEAD,
lock state, or (in full clones) stashes or commits on no remote. Ignored files are listed but do not block.
.IP \(bu 2
A folder that contains a skipped or protected item is itself skipped.
.IP \(bu 2
Symlinks are never followed; nothing outside the canonical root is touched. \fI/\fR, the home directory and
its ancestors, \fI~/Documents\fR, \fI~/Desktop\fR, \fI~/Downloads\fR, \fI~/Library\fR (iCloud, CloudStorage)
and system folders are refused as roots.
.IP \(bu 2
Git runs with fsmonitor, hooks and filter drivers disabled and a scrubbed environment.
.IP \(bu 2
Each item is re\-checked immediately before deletion.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Defaults are built in. \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cleanup/config.toml\fR (default \fI~/.config/cleanup/config.toml\fR)
or \fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR is merged over them. The file must contain \fBversion = 1\fR; unknown keys and
over\-broad patterns are errors. Start from \fBcleanup \-P\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/cleanup/runs.jsonl\fR
Append\-only log of every \fB\-d\fR run (default \fI~/.local/state/cleanup/runs.jsonl\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success, including a dry run.
.TP
\fB1\fR
One or more deletions failed.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Usage, config or root\-guard error.
.TP
\fB130\fR
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBcleanup\fR
Interactive dry run over \fI~/Projects\fR.
.TP
\fBcleanup \-d \-v \-m\fR
Review and delete, including virtualenvs and \fInode_modules\fR.
.TP
\fBcleanup \-T \-d \-f \-o python,rust\fR
Delete Python caches and Rust targets without prompting.
